// Port of the historic Sum2.pms (Delphi generation A, Compiller/): the
// same instruction sequence as Sum.pms, restyled in the comma-group,
// fall-through syntax — the original's `right, if(1, _)` line is a direct
// ancestor of the `.pmc` comma group below. The original's `_` arm (fall
// through to the next statement) has no `.pmc` equivalent, so the check
// names the next line's label explicitly. Same tape contract as sum.pmc:
// numbers are n+1 marks, input "a gap b" with the head on a's first mark,
// output one section a+b. The local functions deliberately shadow
// std::goToEnd/goToBegin — the original carried its own algorithms.
goToEnd() {
 1: right, check(1, 2);
 2: left;
}

goToBegin() {
 1: left, check(1, 2);
 2: right;
}

main() {
    @goToEnd();
    right;
    right;
    @goToEnd();
    unmark;
    left;
    @goToBegin();
    left;
    mark;
    @goToEnd();
    unmark;
    left;
    @goToBegin();
}
